    "behavior": [
      "Spring owns the public routes, explicit response DTOs, query use case, symbol normalization, and transport-neutral full crypto projection",
      "a temporary read-only anti-corruption adapter obtains the legacy calculated projection for BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, and BNB",
      "market regime, profile, market, macro, narrative, bottom-up, moat, supply, on-chain, flows, trend charts, buy score, bottom signal, sizing, verdict, scenarios, and execution bridge fields are preserved",
      "successful catalog and detail projections are fresh for five minutes; a bounded 30-minute stale value is returned immediately while one background refresh per key runs on a virtual thread",
      "the first cold miss and values older than the 30-minute stale ceiling use a blocking single-flight refresh rather than serving stale indefinitely",
      "404, malformed, and unavailable upstream responses are not cached; without a usable stale success, malformed or unavailable responses fail closed with HTTP 502",
      "an inbound serialized-payload cache reuses JSON bytes only while the immutable application projection identity is unchanged",
      "JSON responses of at least 1KB use gzip only when the client negotiates it; identity responses stay byte-exact and gzip responses decode to the same bytes",
      "Spring introduces no local collector, persistence, scheduler, or Telegram side effect; the upstream Node GET can retain its existing route-cache refresh"
    ],
